tasks.spec:
PreMatch:
- Solo setups get a waiting 'pre' stage; online keeps VS -> Vote.
- PreMatch.tsx shows:
  - matchup, AI skill and the stage;
  - 'About 5 min · you defend their possessions' (per-sport EXPECTED_MIN);
  - a Defense control from the defense-pref.ts registry (sport prefs wired at merge);
  - On offer: coins or the capped-day line, rung pack, milestones, Cup prize, SP;
  - <= 3 objective chips;
  - PLAY (56 px; 'LOADING ARENA…' within 100 ms; curtain 'compact' hint) and SIM (hidden for manual-only modes).
- match-how.ts: 'sim' only for a whole-match sim, or when more than 25% of the human's offensive possessions were simmed. Defense Auto/SIM never counts.

Interrupted matches:
- Marker: additive ut.live, written at kickoff and at the first ended possession only.
- Device-local keys: perfect-season:ut-device:v1, and perfect-season:ut-live:v1 written synchronously on hide/pagehide.
- resolveInterrupted:
  - another device under 30 min: left alone;
  - stale: cleared;
  - not started: replayable;
  - otherwise: auto-finish with simRest (simBoth moved out of Match.tsx, seeded, human side -0.15), settled with how 'played' and finish 'auto' (sim-rate SP);
  - at most 2 per ISO week (receipts in hq.claims); beyond that, a forfeit (ff).
- play.ts settle accepts finish auto/forfeit only with the marker id. ClubMatch gets ff/auto.
- The sheet goes through the modal queue. Mode PLAY buttons are inert until the marker is resolved.
- A confirmed solo quit is a forfeit (contract B).
